[{:db/id "q-50044/selection/0747abc7ca85292265cf7bf4573e969a69270142994057a2ba1b4e606a5f8bca" :answer/id #uuid "39c37723-0d69-5949-9392-9e4a22784beb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=6{x}^{3}+8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50044/selection/40bb64b362b4c1f83cb7c121cb7dd2ed5a41ca34443671f63aab467a7c3f9686" :answer/id #uuid "a9fb4249-c501-5987-bf77-623752e67114" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3{x}^{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50044/selection/1105bfa375ec8655124ab53860be61a107a8a22b3fcf8c58135d99506361bd5e" :answer/id #uuid "8506772a-2ec6-5eb3-a530-4e04ad831e12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{x}^{2}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50044/selection/8642d7daef939c210756b5ac5bd982c6ee45d50082a64f6c67e40a3969b4557b" :answer/id #uuid "c99f4f6a-afd7-5903-ab46-48898f42996a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{x}^{3}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50044/selection/08f08cc56fa1d583ab036bdeb3e5ad330cc4baec000ad0aa17095e4d499ac3a3" :answer/id #uuid "f662054e-567a-5206-baa6-0c106c3270f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50044/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0367d76d-393f-563b-8a18-a5ef095afd09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50044/selection/8642d7daef939c210756b5ac5bd982c6ee45d50082a64f6c67e40a3969b4557b" :answer-field/choices ["q-50044/selection/0747abc7ca85292265cf7bf4573e969a69270142994057a2ba1b4e606a5f8bca" "q-50044/selection/40bb64b362b4c1f83cb7c121cb7dd2ed5a41ca34443671f63aab467a7c3f9686" "q-50044/selection/1105bfa375ec8655124ab53860be61a107a8a22b3fcf8c58135d99506361bd5e" "q-50044/selection/8642d7daef939c210756b5ac5bd982c6ee45d50082a64f6c67e40a3969b4557b" "q-50044/selection/08f08cc56fa1d583ab036bdeb3e5ad330cc4baec000ad0aa17095e4d499ac3a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50044" :question/id #uuid "1eb154da-4739-51ad-b420-cb4dc79403e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-50044" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=2$\n \n\n$$\nx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6{x}^{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=2{x}^{3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(-1)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =2(-1)^{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =-2+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{3}+4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-50044/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50044"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-50148"] :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{e}^{3x}=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}\\,{e}^{3x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79565/selection/520208a41b16aa5f125c6a643a592d49b854a4311f4def084d11ecffb718e174" :answer/id #uuid "ce5a1a22-4b15-5473-b750-1020ede68b95" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/ff60bb4fceb52346f5f9b4275343729a737dd52e0283beaaeb4d740e1751feca.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79565/selection/8853eff47225e4f9f6900e1b8ef0305c9b5520628187bd687041f74a6757a838" :answer/id #uuid "38afabcd-d507-5b5e-83a5-9dec681cd7cc" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/09fb3125c260d2f042ec3a509bb7e776d0d47ece3e78255931f8bc9781aa31c8.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79565/selection/c3f9f29bc331a5d7883b8f9574ff2050e08391f67af7c95ad5e20bf7d8aa2636" :answer/id #uuid "2d89dbb7-8700-51aa-a90e-9804c52e79c5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/8ca894c5a5ca9e93af8c39242ba1584447472bb81c872e1225c52a4fbc652e1c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79565/selection/94017568cc2b9d15a46fd9e18ba6a8b0373859c35779bd6c19cd1bdfd5763560" :answer/id #uuid "50b3afae-2b5a-5d32-9f05-62decfb8aa63" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/af10bb7e5a91561be6d83950803920c8c74aeee40f7982c0564250f707628cbb.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79565/selection/b820c00a5c0d0ae28877dea60ac7196699f3ae152d75e4370a34b732a24f6335" :answer/id #uuid "bd8980fd-0ff7-5beb-bc78-02a616ebdf40" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/9908bd23538332705791bbd968dfdf5e22ddde8884aaa9fed58268bc1132d208.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79565/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "10e6a4ef-c119-5032-a4c4-9df0295af8c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79565/selection/94017568cc2b9d15a46fd9e18ba6a8b0373859c35779bd6c19cd1bdfd5763560" :answer-field/choices ["q-79565/selection/520208a41b16aa5f125c6a643a592d49b854a4311f4def084d11ecffb718e174" "q-79565/selection/8853eff47225e4f9f6900e1b8ef0305c9b5520628187bd687041f74a6757a838" "q-79565/selection/c3f9f29bc331a5d7883b8f9574ff2050e08391f67af7c95ad5e20bf7d8aa2636" "q-79565/selection/94017568cc2b9d15a46fd9e18ba6a8b0373859c35779bd6c19cd1bdfd5763560" "q-79565/selection/b820c00a5c0d0ae28877dea60ac7196699f3ae152d75e4370a34b732a24f6335"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79565" :question/id #uuid "b7716424-9b11-538f-a06b-55bd73654360" :question/math-academy-id "q-79565" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/fa13b048e5ca54c7074bbf6ec11421bfd8fb9e1618abd732a5faa1d78372a863.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79565/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79565"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347842/field-1/61e33e0a287e4aaf44a0da7d4b3a7da826cfe547c804e79a0ed7d680de3d0624" :answer/id #uuid "ec6175a2-7628-54e2-9a83-5ea329ef75ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x^2-\\frac{25}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347842/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc032f3-fbc1-54cb-8244-03c727fb366d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347842/field-1/61e33e0a287e4aaf44a0da7d4b3a7da826cfe547c804e79a0ed7d680de3d0624" :answer-field/choices ["q-347842/field-1/61e33e0a287e4aaf44a0da7d4b3a7da826cfe547c804e79a0ed7d680de3d0624"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347842" :question/id #uuid "85b460c5-45ef-565d-85f6-70fe7fc6f047" :question/math-academy-id "q-347842" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $8x-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=5.$\n\n$y=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,+${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{x}^{2}+8x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(2)=5$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C \\\\ 5 & =-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+4({2}^{2})+C \\\\ 5 & =-\\frac{8}{3}+16+C \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{40}{3}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{25}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}-\\frac{25}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-347842/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347842"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
